Bisecting the `bad in naddr: REGPAIR' fault into one cc/ file
=============================================================

WHERE THE HUNT STANDS

`sys/lib/tests/regpair-min.c' is ten lines -- two structs and
`d->offset = s->size', both members `vlong' -- and APExp's 8c cannot
compile it.  Current 9front's 8c can.  So can every 64-bit backend.

`sys/src/cmd/8cu' settled which half: it is UPSTREAM's 8c linked
against APExp's cc.a, and **it fails too**.  So the fault is in this
directory, and the four non-rename differences in our own 8c are
cleared by measurement rather than by reading.

FIVE HYPOTHESES ARE DEAD, each by a run rather than an argument:

	two register pairs live at once	regpair-probe case 7
	the two structs differing	case 14 (same types, reversed)
	the member name			case 15
	position in the file		-DLEADER
	the OAS lvalue bypass		the addable notice never fired

That last one is worth keeping in mind: `com.c's OAS skips `tlvalue'
for ONAME/OIND/ODOT/OBIT, and `tlvalue' does nothing but test
`addable' -- so the exemption looked like it could hand the backend a
node it knew was not addressable.  **The notice says `addable' is 1,
so it cannot.**

WHAT THIS DIRECTORY CONTAINS FOR THE NEXT STEP

`com.c.9front' is upstream 9front's `com.c' at 38c61773c, verbatim.
Swapping it in is the next bisection step, and it is a real one rather
than a guess: `com.c' is where the tree is type-checked and where
`addable' is set, it is the largest single difference from upstream in
this directory, and it is one of only four files here that CAN be
swapped.  `dcl.c', `lex.c', `sub.c' and `cc.y' all reference `Spec'
upstream -- the 2026-06-10 declaration-specifier refactor APExp does
not have -- so upstream's copies of those will not compile here at all.

Checked before shipping, in both directions:

  - the only function our `com.c' defines that upstream's does not is
    `boolnorm', and it is `static', so nothing outside the file wants
    it;
  - every function upstream's `com.c' calls exists in this tree.

So it ought to build.  It has NOT been built -- kencc's sources need
Plan 9's <u.h>, so the first build of anything here is the VM's.

HOW TO RUN IT

	cd sys/src/cmd/cc
	cp com.c com.c.apexp
	cp com.c.9front com.c
	mk install
	cd ../8c && mk install
	cd ../../../lib/tests && 8c regpair-min.c

	# and to go back
	cd sys/src/cmd/cc && cp com.c.apexp com.c && mk install
	cd ../8c && mk install

  it COMPILES -> the fault is in our `com.c', 1507 lines, and the
                 next bisection is within one file instead of ten.
  it FAILS    -> `com.c' is cleared, and what is left is `scon.c',
                 `pgen.c', `pswt.c' (also swappable) and the four
                 Spec-entangled ones, which need the merge before they
                 can be tested this way.

READ THE LINE NUMBER.  `regpair-min.c's assignment is on line 101.
Any other line means the file under test is not the one you think it
is -- that has already happened once here and cost a round.

AND EXPECT THE SWAP TO COST FEATURES, NOT JUST THE BUG.  Upstream's
`com.c' has none of APExp's complex-number handling, no `boolnorm',
and no VLA `sizeof' rewriting, so a tree built with it will fail
elsewhere.  **This is a diagnostic, not a candidate fix**, and the
restore line above is part of the procedure rather than an
afterthought.
